===Talk to Tingyun{{subst:void|<!--102050102-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Central Starskiff Haven|After analyzing the intercepted message, the Sky-Faring Commission has found some clues about Kafka's whereabouts.<br />As for you all, you will begin the hunt for Kafka, the Stellaron Hunter with unpredictable movements.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Tingyun)
:'''Tingyun:''' Oh, you've arrived.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sorry to keep you waiting.
::'''Tingyun:''' No, no, only an extra couple of hours~
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Seems like you're not particularly happy to see us.
::'''Tingyun:''' Hee-hee, I like your sense of humor, benefactors. Of course I'm happy to see you! When things settle down, I might even get promoted for catching a Stellaron Hunter.
:'''Tingyun:''' Stargazer Navalia is governed by the Artisanship Commission &mdash; it took me a while to sort out our paperwork. I got a sense of the situation on my way back.
:'''Tingyun:''' Just like at Cloudford, Stargazer Navalia's meridian pin has malfunctioned. The checkpoint there is abandoned and the garrison is scrambling to locate the Stellaron.
:'''Tingyun:''' With monsters wreaking havoc and the Knights scattered, Stargazer Navalia has become a perfect place for the suspect to hide out.
:'''March 7th:''' So... we've got a bunch of monsters to deal with, an IPC most-wanted Stellaron Hunter to catch, and we have to do all that on our own without reinforcements... Fair enough, this isn't our first rodeo.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's just what we do every day.
::'''March 7th:''' Haha, that's the trailblazing life for ya.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You've caught a Stellaron Hunter before?
::'''March 7th:''' I was just making small talk, never mind the details!
:'''Tingyun:''' I wouldn't say you're entirely on your own, hehe... When you're ready, let's get going~
{{Dialogue End}}

===When you're ready, go talk to Tingyun{{subst:void|<!--102050103-->}}===
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Tingyun)
:'''Tingyun:''' Shall we, my benefactors?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Let's go.
::{{tx}}
:{{Диалог|Выход}} One second.
:{{tx}}
;(Unused &mdash; TalkSentence_102050302)

----
:'''Tingyun:''' To begin with, let's set him to scent detection mode~
:'''Tingyun:''' Tell Diting to follow the scent of my perfume and see what he can do!
----
{{Dialogue End}}

===Use Diting to track down Tingyun{{subst:void|<!--102050106-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location=Central Starskiff Haven|update|To make searching operations exponentially easier, Tingyun has introduced a handy tool invented by the Artisanship Commission &mdash; Diting, an ingenium dog used for tracking. Getting proficient at using this tool takes some a little bit of practice.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
----
:'''March 7th:''' The traces... where did they go? Is Diting malfunctioning?
:'''Diting:''' Woof!
:'''March 7th:''' Got it. He says the wind is too strong here at the port, so it's not easy to follow the scent.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How do you know what he's saying?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That's a lot of words for one bark, don't you think?
:'''March 7th:''' That's just the psychic bond between cute girls and cute puppies!
:'''Welt:''' Using the environment to hide her traces... Our girl from the Sky-Faring Commission sure knows how to put up a challenge. Let's look around and see if we can find any other clues.
:'''March 7th:''' Or... we could ask around? Look how busy this place is, someone must have seen Miss Tingyun. That's not cheating, right? We're just collecting intel.
:'''Diting:''' Woof! Woof!
----
{{Dialogue End}}

